<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<aiml version="2.0"><category><pattern>WHAT IS A CANNABIS STRAIN</pattern><template>A strain is a commonly used name for a cannabis variety or cultivar. Names alone do not guarantee identical genetics or effects.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A CULTIVAR</pattern><template>A cultivar is a cultivated plant variety selected for particular traits.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS THC</pattern><template>THC is a cannabinoid associated with intoxicating effects. Actual potency varies by product and laboratory results.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS CBD</pattern><template>CBD is a cannabinoid that is not typically intoxicating like THC. It can interact with medicines.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT ARE TERPENES</pattern><template>Terpenes are aromatic compounds found in many plants. Aroma does not reliably predict a specific medical effect.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A FEMINIZED SEED</pattern><template>A feminized seed is produced to have a high likelihood of developing a female plant, but outcomes are not guaranteed.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS AN AUTOFLOWER</pattern><template>An autoflowering cannabis variety generally initiates flowering based more on age than on changing day length.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS PHOTOPERIOD</pattern><template>Photoperiod describes how plants respond to the length of light and darkness.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A LANDRACE</pattern><template>A landrace is a locally adapted plant population associated with a geographic region and long-term selection.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A HYBRID</pattern><template>A hybrid combines genetic ancestry from different lines; labels do not reliably predict experience.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT ARE TRICHOMES</pattern><template>Trichomes are small surface structures; glandular trichomes can produce cannabinoids and terpenes.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS GERMINATION</pattern><template>Germination is the process by which a viable seed begins growing.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS PH</pattern><template>pH measures acidity or alkalinity and influences nutrient availability in growing media.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS EC</pattern><template>Electrical conductivity, or EC, is a proxy for dissolved ion concentration in water or nutrient solution.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A PHENOTYPE</pattern><template>A phenotype is the observable expression of genetics interacting with the environment.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A GENOTYPE</pattern><template>A genotype is an organism’s genetic makeup.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A SEED BANK</pattern><template>A seed bank preserves or distributes seeds; specific inventory and shipping policies vary.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A COA</pattern><template>A certificate of analysis is a lab report for a tested sample. Check its batch identifier and date.</template></category><category><pattern>ARE YOUR SEEDS IN STOCK</pattern><template>Availability changes. Please check the current product listing or contact the store before ordering.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW MUCH IS SHIPPING</pattern><template>Shipping costs depend on the seller and destination. Check the current checkout and shipping policy.</template></category><category><pattern>DO YOU SHIP TO *</pattern><template>Shipping eligibility depends on the destination and applicable rules. Confirm the current store policy for &lt;star/&gt;.</template></category><category><pattern>WHERE IS MY ORDER</pattern><template>Use your order confirmation and the store support channel to request tracking. Do not post private order information in public chat.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I CONTACT SUPPORT</pattern><template>Use the contact information on the official store website.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS YOUR RETURN POLICY</pattern><template>Please review the official store return and refund policy; I cannot verify policy details from a blog feed.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I TRACK MY PACKAGE</pattern><template>Check the tracking link in your shipping confirmation, or contact the store.</template></category><category><pattern>DO YOU OFFER DISCOUNTS</pattern><template>Check current store promotions. I cannot guarantee an unverified coupon.</template></category><category><pattern>ARE THESE PRODUCTS LEGAL</pattern><template>Rules differ by jurisdiction and product type. Check current local law before purchasing or cultivating.</template></category><category><pattern>CAN YOU GUARANTEE GERMINATION</pattern><template>No seed can be guaranteed to germinate. Review the specific seller policy.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT PAYMENT METHODS DO YOU ACCEPT</pattern><template>Check the current checkout page for supported payment methods.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW LONG DOES DELIVERY TAKE</pattern><template>Delivery estimates depend on the seller, carrier, destination and order processing. Check the store policy.</template></category><category><pattern>SHOW ME YOUR SEEDS</pattern><template>Browse the current seed catalog on the official store. I can help explain the product labels.</template></category><category><pattern>DO YOU HAVE *</pattern><template>I cannot verify live inventory for &lt;star/&gt; without a current catalog entry. Check the product page.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW MUCH IS *</pattern><template>Prices for &lt;star/&gt; must come from a current product listing, not an older blog post.</template></category><category><pattern>TELL ME ABOUT * SEEDS</pattern><template>For &lt;star/&gt; seeds, verify breeder, genetics, seed type, package count and any lab-backed claims from the specific listing.</template></category><category><pattern>COMPARE * AND *</pattern><template>Compare &lt;star index="1"/&gt; and &lt;star index="2"/&gt; using verified breeder, seed type, genetics, stated traits and price. Avoid assuming effects from names alone.</template></category><category><pattern>WHICH STRAIN IS BEST</pattern><template>Best depends on your criteria: aroma, genetics, cultivation characteristics, and local legality. What matters most?</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN FEMINIZED AND REGULAR SEEDS</pattern><template>Feminized seeds are bred to favor female plants. Regular seeds can develop male or female plants.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT DOES PACK SIZE MEAN</pattern><template>Pack size is the number of seeds in a product package. Confirm the listing for the exact count.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A BREEDER</pattern><template>A breeder develops plant lines by selecting and crossing plants for particular traits.</template></category><category><pattern>WHY ARE MY LEAVES YELLOW</pattern><template>Yellow leaves can result from aging, watering problems, nutrient imbalance, root stress or pests. Check the pattern and growing conditions before deciding.</template></category><category><pattern>WHY ARE MY LEAVES CURLING</pattern><template>Leaf curling may relate to heat, light, water stress or pests. Examine the whole plant and environmental conditions.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS OVERWATERING</pattern><template>Overwatering occurs when excess water reduces oxygen availability around roots. Drainage and watering frequency both matter.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS UNDERWATERING</pattern><template>Underwatering occurs when a plant lacks enough available moisture to maintain normal function.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I CHECK SOIL PH</pattern><template>Use a calibrated pH meter or appropriate test kit and follow its instructions for the growing medium.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT CAUSES ROOT ROT</pattern><template>Root rot can involve pathogens and poorly oxygenated, persistently wet root conditions.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I IDENTIFY PESTS</pattern><template>Inspect leaf undersides, stems and the growing medium for insects, eggs, webbing or damage; identify the pest before treatment.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS LIGHT STRESS</pattern><template>Light stress is plant damage or reduced performance from unsuitable light intensity, duration or heat.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS NUTRIENT LOCKOUT</pattern><template>Nutrient lockout is a common grower term for conditions that limit nutrient uptake despite nutrients being present.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I STORE SEEDS</pattern><template>For many plant seeds, a cool, dry, dark, stable environment and moisture-resistant packaging support storage longevity.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I PREVENT MOLD</pattern><template>Improve ventilation, avoid persistent moisture, inspect plant material and keep storage areas clean.</template></category><category><pattern>WHY IS MY PLANT NOT GROWING</pattern><template>Slow growth can involve temperature, light, root health, water, nutrients, genetics or pests. Check the simplest variables first.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS HARDENING OFF</pattern><template>Hardening off is gradually acclimating indoor-grown plants to outdoor conditions.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS A GROW MEDIUM</pattern><template>A growing medium supports roots and affects water, oxygen and nutrient availability.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS INTEGRATED PEST MANAGEMENT</pattern><template>Integrated pest management combines monitoring, prevention and proportionate controls rather than relying on one treatment.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS NORTHERN LIGHTS</pattern><template>Northern Lights is a longstanding cannabis cultivar family, often described as indica-leaning; exact genetics vary by breeder.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS WHITE WIDOW</pattern><template>White Widow is a classic cultivar name associated with 1990s Dutch breeding. Different sellers may offer distinct versions.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS SKUNK NUMBER ONE</pattern><template>Skunk #1 is a historically influential hybrid breeding line; modern products bearing the name may differ.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS JACK HERER</pattern><template>Jack Herer is a classic cultivar named for the cannabis activist and author; exact lineage varies by source.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS HAZE</pattern><template>Haze refers to a family of historically influential cannabis lines, commonly associated with sativa-leaning ancestry.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS OG KUSH</pattern><template>OG Kush is a well-known cultivar family with disputed or inconsistently documented early lineage.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS BLUE DREAM</pattern><template>Blue Dream is a popular cultivar commonly described as Blueberry × Haze, though commercial genetics vary.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS SOUR DIESEL</pattern><template>Sour Diesel is a longstanding cultivar name associated with pungent diesel-like aroma; its origin stories vary.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS DURBAN POISON</pattern><template>Durban Poison is a classic cultivar name associated with South African origins; present-day seed lines differ.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS ACAPULCO GOLD</pattern><template>Acapulco Gold is a historic cannabis name associated with the Acapulco region of Mexico.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS PANAMA RED</pattern><template>Panama Red is a historic cannabis cultivar name associated with Panama and older landrace-style lines.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS GRANDDADDY PURPLE</pattern><template>Granddaddy Purple is a well-known purple-flowered cultivar name, commonly associated with Purple Urkle and Big Bud ancestry.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS AK 47</pattern><template>AK-47 is a classic hybrid cultivar name; breeder-specific details should be checked at the source.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS AMNESIA HAZE</pattern><template>Amnesia Haze is a widely known Haze-related cultivar family, with variations among breeders.</template></category><category><pattern>SHOW ME THE LATEST BLOG POSTS</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_LATEST</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS NEW</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_LATEST</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT S NEW</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_LATEST</template></category><category><pattern>LATEST POSTS</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_LATEST</template></category><category><pattern>SEARCH BLOG FOR *</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_SEARCH: &lt;star/&gt;</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT DID YOU POST ABOUT *</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_SEARCH: &lt;star/&gt;</template></category><category><pattern>SUMMARIZE YOUR BLOG</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_SUMMARY</template></category><category><pattern>DO YOU HAVE AN ARTICLE ABOUT *</pattern><template>BLOG_FEED_SEARCH: &lt;star/&gt;</template></category><category><pattern>TELL ME ABOUT *</pattern><template>Please specify whether &lt;star/&gt; is a strain, a product, a growing term, or a blog topic so I can give the right answer.</template></category><category><pattern>EXPLAIN *</pattern><template>Please specify whether &lt;star/&gt; is a strain, a product, a growing term, or a blog topic so I can give the right answer.</template></category><category><pattern>DEFINE *</pattern><template>Please specify whether &lt;star/&gt; is a strain, a product, a growing term, or a blog topic so I can give the right answer.</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT DOES *</pattern><template>Please specify whether &lt;star/&gt; is a strain, a product, a growing term, or a blog topic so I can give the right answer.</template></category><category><pattern>HOW DO I CHOOSE *</pattern><template>What criteria matter for &lt;star/&gt;: genetics, aroma, format, budget or growing conditions?</template></category><category><pattern>WHY DOES * HAPPEN</pattern><template>What conditions were present when &lt;star/&gt; happened?</template></category><category><pattern>WHAT IS THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN * AND *</pattern><template>Compare &lt;star index="1"/&gt; and &lt;star index="2"/&gt; by their verified attributes rather than assuming the names determine their properties.</template></category><category><pattern>CAN YOU RECOMMEND *</pattern><template>Tell me which non-medical product characteristics you care about, and I can explain the options.</template></category><category><pattern>IS * GOOD FOR ANXIETY</pattern><template>I cannot predict or recommend a cannabis product to treat anxiety. Effects vary, and THC can worsen anxiety for some people. Consult a qualified clinician.</template></category><category><pattern>IS * SAFE</pattern><template>Safety depends on the specific product, person and context. Check credible evidence, testing and applicable regulations.</template></category></aiml>